<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ravning Bridge</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 980</span> · Also known as Ravning Enge bridge</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ravning Bridge was a wooden bridge across the meadows of the Vejle river valley at Ravning Enge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. Tree-ring dating places its construction around 980, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-bluetooth">Harald Bluetooth</a>. About 760 metres long and 5 metres wide, supported by more than a thousand oak posts, it was the longest bridge in Denmark until the twentieth century, yet it was used for only a short time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ravning-bridge.jpg" alt="Ravning Bridge" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Beethoven9 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ravningbroen.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
